Personality sym102 (Symbian OS 10.1 FP2, Nokia Belle FP2; 701 RM-774 113.010.1506, 808 RM-807 113.010.1508):
exec tables KExec102* (personalities/sym102/exec.map, generated into execpers_map.h), registry number 7. The
sym101 numbering with three calls inserted (S11, S12, Sd8) and Belle's Sd6/Sd7 gone; the same user side
conventions as sym101 (TLocalThreadData layout, nested library attach) [inferred: same EUser line].
Loader structures: TCodeSegCreateInfo has 4 more bytes (ExecLoaderCodeSegUserSize = 476), so
TProcessCreateInfo's own fields are read and written 4 bytes further on (in the base's tail padding). FP2's
loader passes iUseCodePaging = 2 for code it does not page: read as "not paged", given back as 2. Trace builds
(KDLL) dump the raw words 352..480 of each code segment's info (CSRAW).

ExecLoaderCodeSegUserSize is where TProcessCreateInfo's own fields start in the loader's structure, so 9.1 sets
it too (380, = its copy size; left at 472 the N73's priority read as 0 and every ProcessCreate failed with
KErrArgument). The paging mode 2 handling has its own flag (ExecLoaderPagingMode2, FP2 only).
